---
title: Sukka Lamb
description: A very tasty dry curry, inspired by Cottenham Curry Palace
author: Alexander Thoukydides
servings: 6
prep time: 30m
cook time: 3h45m
course: Main
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Indian
tags:
- indian
- main-course
- savoury
- meat
---

= Braise =

Place the @lamb leg{1%kg}(cut into large chunks), @onion{1%medium}(finely chopped), @ginger{2%inch}(finely chopped), and @garlic{10%cloves} in a #casserole dish with lid{}.

Mix the spices (@turmeric{2%tsp}, @ground coriander{4%tsp}, @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}(freshly ground), @garam masala{1%tsp}, and @salt{pinch}) into the @water{100%ml} and @yoghurt{3%tbsp}.

Pour the sauce over the lamb, fit the lid, and simmer at 150°C for 2.5 to ~{3%hours} until the lamb is incredibly tender.

Remove the lid and let most of the remaining liquid bubble for ~{30%minutes}.

= Stir Fry =

Heat the @vegetable oil{3%tbsp} in a medium-hot frying pan. Add the @bell peppers{3}(cut into thick strips) and @finger chillies{20}(cut diagonally, seeds left in), and stir-fry for ~{2%minutes}.

Add the @onions{3%medium}(cut into wedges) and spices (@ground coriander{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{0.5%tsp}, @garam masala{0.5%tsp}, and @mustard powder{1%tsp}), and fry for ~{15%seconds}.

Add the lamb with all remaining liquid and increase the heat to high. Stir fry until dry and the meat is glazed and browned.